 "about": "Every World Championship event from 1886 to 2024 that the game library covers. `name` is the title the event is shown under (its year is added). Matches list the two players, title holder or first-named first; tournaments list the winner. Excluded on purpose: 1975 (Fischer forfeited and no games were played); the 1909 Lasker - Janowski exhibition match (not played for the title); and the FIDE knockout events of 1997, 1998 (including its Karpov - Anand final), 1999, 2000, 2002 and 2004, whose short knockout format is not the championship match or tournament the rest of the roster follows. From 1993 to 2004 the title was split: the PCA/Classical line (Kasparov, then Kramnik) and the FIDE line both appear; 2006 reunified it.",
